<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An anomalous old Model T with the ability to traverse anything, physically possible or not, that always comes back to where it was previously parked, always with souvenir.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The narrative given within the articles would detail how the car was first found, the surprise when researchers first found out it missing, the tests it underwent before researchers understood it better, and the later investigation when researchers realized it was actually traveling to places around the world, and ending with how the final containment procedures came about to keep in permanently in place.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The automobile's first disappearance with tire marks leading into a concrete wall, the realization that it really was just taking a straight path from its containment to its desired destination, and the odd descriptions of its sightings, often including the appearance of a man in a brown suit and bowler hat.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I tried to pitch this SCP a year ago and was shut down by the only reviewer that interacted with me, who at first asked that I revise it, then never responded to my revision. I lost the motivation to try further for a bit given the sour interaction, but I just couldn't stay away from SCP. Hopefully this time things go better. I'm willing to listen to feedback, I just don't want to be forgotten.</p>

