					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/owltamer" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5409628); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5409628&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606056696" alt="Owltamer" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5409628)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/owltamer" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5409628); return false;" >Owltamer</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606020367 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Nov 2020 04:46</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825108">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Starting&nbsp;'er&nbsp;up...</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Nevermind,&nbsp;they're&nbsp;watching</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Ok, so as of right now, I'm thinking that the car (or rather, our resident suited fellow) will refuse to leave if being directly observed or recorded visually. It is, however, possible to track the car with something like GPS, and even possible to record audio on or around the car, in which case the sounds that would be recorded could include: the engine revving up, the car peeling out, sounds from the cars immediate environment but never including collision despite the cars route. I hadn't considered GPS till reading your message about cameras. GPS would just show the car taking a straight path to it's destination. I'm still mulling over whether I think the suited man would leave the devices planted on the car be longer than one trip, having subsequent trips begin with the removal of said devices.</p>
<p>I'm very glad to hear the foundation would be game for testing the anomalous properties despite their including the car leaving temporarily. This makes things much easier. I think that once the foundation has a better grasp of how the car works, it will be easy to contain, only really needing surveillance, which will keep it where it is 99% of the time (I'm planning on having a single log where video footage cuts out suddenly, and the cameras to the car's containment being damaged). The majority of logs will be either before the foundation has a grasp of what is going on, and in tests where they intend to try to control the situation to the best of their ability.</p>
<p>Where do I go from here? Maybe its selfish to be asking you because I feel like there is probably a guide on this somewhere, but I'm still trying to understand this all. Is this the stage where I start actually writing the logs and article? Do I just need to be able to explain my idea in a more solid way? I know there will be more steps before its done (obviously) but I'm not 100% certain of what my current step is.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Again, thank you for the feedback. I really mean it. I feel like I have trouble taking criticism sometimes, and am trying to get over that flaw of mine, but I haven't had any issues with that yet. I feel like your input has brought me much closer to understanding my own SCP, and has guided the way I've looked at this project. So thanks</p>

							</div>

								
					
